    "created_at": "2026-03-12T13:32:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-12T13:32:46Z",
    "body": "> > maybe we can assert that it's always enabled because how else would you enter the fragment parser?\n> \n> In our WordPress parser we use the fragment parser predominantly and work exclusively with scripting disabled. This work dovetails the streaming out-of-order work being discussed because of implications on things like `<noscript>` and the way that the fragment parsing algorithm is able to create invalid DOM that is unrepresentable in HTML.\n> \n> Maybe what we are doing is somehow not spec-compliant, but in a text-text world instead of text-DOM (in the browser) the fragment parsing is more important since we are usually working on the server with pieces of HTML outside of full documents.\n\nThanks for this feedback! This issue is about fixing a spec bug in this area so that we can allow scripting in fragment parsing etc without breaking stuff 😁",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
